{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788350783,"nonce":"5IKFFEAkD7zfoiN5uhdp3nrwn5c=","title":"Run `m1-20260901`: `digest.construction.awaiting_materials` sat at **exactly 22 for fifteen straight in-game days** (day 40 to day 55). The agent read it every turn and nothing ever said the number was not moving. That stalled set contained the freezer, and the freezer is why the colony had no larder.","message":"`ConstructionVerbs.Section(map)` publishes `awaiting_materials` as a scalar count. A scalar tells you the size of the set, never its age. Fifteen identical reads and one read are the same envelope, so \"stalled\" is only visible to a caller that keeps its own history across days — which no checklist requires and no observer provides.\n\nThe per-element rows have the same gap: `{\"def\":\"Heater\",\"state\":\"awaiting-materials\",\"missing\":[...]}` carries no indication of how long it has been in that state.\n\n\nThe agent could bank yesterday's count. It did not, and asking it to is the failure mode `read-every-return-or-lose-a-colonist` was written about: a derived fact that only exists if the caller remembers to derive it will eventually not be derived. The mod holds the tick and can hold the transition; `AgentGameComponent` is the existing home for state that must persist across reads.\n\n\n1. Each unresolved `construction` element publishes when it entered its current state: `state_since_tick` and `state_age_ticks`. An element that changes state resets it. This makes \"flat across N days\" answerable from a single read.\n2. `digest.construction` gains a `stalled[]` roll-up: elements whose state has been `awaiting-materials` or `blocked` across **\u003e= 2 day boundaries**, each naming `def`, `at`, `layout_id` where one applies, and the missing material or blocker. A count alone repeats this defect.\n3. The report distinguishes **awaiting a material that exists on the map** from **awaiting a material that does not**. This run had 30 unforbidden reachable `ComponentIndustrial` while an element reported short of 1. Coordinate with `e08c3e5` item 3, which adds the skill-gate branch to the same triage; the two must not each invent a different vocabulary for \"why is there no worker\".\n4. `checklists/turn.md` gains the trip-wire, keyed to the day-boundary read, citing the field by name. A lesson no checklist cites is half-landed.\n5. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-stalled-build.py` on a bench: place a blueprint short of a material, advance across two day boundaries, assert it appears in `stalled[]` naming the def and the missing material; supply the material, advance, assert it leaves.\n\n\nThis is item 3 of the repair round's bench list: *leave a blueprint short of materials across two day boundaries, it is reported as stalled, naming the def and the missing material.*","files":null}]}